---
import LocationLayout from '../layouts/LocationLayout.astro';
import { locationsBySlug } from '../data/locations';

const location = locationsBySlug['queen-annes-county'];
---

<LocationLayout 
  location={location}
  title="Personal Injury Lawyer in Queen Anne's County | Alex Poberesky Law"
  description="Experienced personal injury and criminal defense attorney serving Queen Anne's County, Maryland. Free consultation. Call (410) 484-0400."
>
  <h2>Experienced Legal Representation in Queen Anne's County, Maryland</h2>
  
  <p>
    Queen Anne's County serves as the gateway to Maryland's Eastern Shore, with the Bay Bridge 
    connecting it to the Baltimore-Washington metropolitan area. This strategic location brings 
    heavy traffic, especially during summer months, creating increased risk of accidents. 
    Attorney Alex Poberesky provides dedicated legal representation to Queen Anne's County residents.
  </p>
  
  <h3>Personal Injury Cases in Queen Anne's County</h3>
  
  <p>
    The Chesapeake Bay Bridge carries millions of vehicles annually, making the Route 50/301 
    corridor through Queen Anne's County one of the most heavily traveled in the state. 
    Accidents on this corridor and throughout the county can cause serious injuries. We help 
    victims recover the compensation they deserve.
  </p>
  
  <p>We handle personal injury cases throughout Queen Anne's County, including:</p>
  
  <ul>
    <li>Car accidents on Routes 50, 301, and 213</li>
    <li>Truck and commercial vehicle accidents</li>
    <li>Bay Bridge-related accidents</li>
    <li>Motorcycle accidents</li>
    <li>Boating accidents on the Chesapeake Bay and Chester River</li>
    <li>Agricultural and farm equipment accidents</li>
    <li>Slip and fall accidents at businesses and outlets</li>
    <li>Wrongful death cases</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h3>Criminal Defense in Queen Anne's County</h3>
  
  <p>
    Whether you're a resident or were passing through Queen Anne's County when you were arrested, 
    you need experienced legal defense. We represent clients facing DUI charges, drug offenses, 
    assault, theft, and other criminal matters in the Queen Anne's County courts.
  </p>
  
  <h3>Convenient Access from Both Shores</h3>
  
  <p>
    Our Pikesville office is easily accessible from Queen Anne's County via the Bay Bridge. 
    We also travel to the Eastern Shore to meet with clients and appear in court. With over 
    26 years of experience, we provide the skilled representation you need.
  </p>
  
  <h3>Serving All Queen Anne's County Communities</h3>
  
  <p>
    We represent clients throughout Queen Anne's County, including Centreville, Grasonville, 
    Stevensville, Chester, Queenstown, Church Hill, and surrounding areas. Contact us today 
    for a free consultation.
  </p>
</LocationLayout>
